This project wraps and depends on several open-source tools and libraries.
None are bundled in this repository; install instructions in INSTALL_GUIDE.md
and the upstream projects retain their own licenses.

EDA tools (invoked by mcp-eda, typically inside the
hpretl/iic-osic-tools Docker image):

  - Yosys                  ISC License        https://yosyshq.net/yosys/
  - Verilator              LGPLv3 / Artistic  https://www.veripool.org/verilator/
  - Icarus Verilog         GPLv2+ / LGPL      http://iverilog.icarus.com/
  - SymbiYosys (sby)       ISC License        https://github.com/YosysHQ/sby
  - OpenROAD               BSD-3-Clause       https://theopenroadproject.org/
  - OpenSTA                GPLv3              https://github.com/parallaxsw/OpenSTA
  - KLayout                GPLv3              https://www.klayout.de/
  - Magic                  BSD-style          http://opencircuitdesign.com/magic/
  - Netgen                 GPL                http://opencircuitdesign.com/netgen/
  - Xschem                 GPLv2              https://xschem.sourceforge.io/
  - ngspice                BSD-3-Clause       https://ngspice.sourceforge.io/
  - cocotb                 BSD-3-Clause       https://www.cocotb.org/

MCP SDK and Node.js runtime:

  - @modelcontextprotocol/sdk    MIT          https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/sdk
  - Node.js                      MIT          https://nodejs.org/

PDKs supported (each retains its own license; not bundled):

  - SkyWater PDK (sky130A / sky130B)   Apache-2.0
  - GlobalFoundries 180nm MCU (gf180mcu)   Apache-2.0
  - IHP Open PDK (ihp130)              Apache-2.0

FPGA toolchains (host-side, proprietary; not bundled):

  - Intel Quartus Prime Lite Edition (free)
  - AMD Vivado / ISE (free editions)

Reference hardware mentioned in documentation:

  - Terasic DE10-Lite (MAX10 FPGA development board)
  - Keysight DSO-X 3014T (oscilloscope, SCPI over USB-TMC)

